A **private limited company**:

- prohibits invitations to the public to subscribe for shares, debentures or deposits;
- needs minimum paid up capital of **one lakh rupees**, with **two to two hundred shareholders**;
- must end its name with **Pvt. Ltd**;
- has shares that are not traded in the open market;
- limits shareholders' liability to their investment;
- needs the Memorandum of Association, Articles of Association and Certificate of Incorporation to commence business.
